    "offer": "The Act would let a person request medical help to die only if two independent doctors confirm they are 18 or older, a New Zealand citizen or resident, suffering from a terminal illness likely to end their life within six months, in an advanced state of irreversible physical decline, experiencing unbearable suffering, and able to make an informed choice. If either doctor doubts the person's mental competence, a psychiatrist must also assess them. Any sign of pressure or coercion halts the process; doctors who object on conscience grounds may opt out. The eligible person chooses the timing and method, and a doctor prepares or administers the lethal dose.",
