        "text": "Supporters note that Oregon has run tightly regulated physician-assisted dying since 1997 under a near-identical framework — a six-month prognosis, two independent doctors and capacity checks — and argue its safeguards have kept the law confined to a small, clearly defined group rather than opening a slippery slope.",
