    "problem": "Before this law, Texas permitted abortion until about 20 weeks of pregnancy. On an ultrasound, electrical cardiac activity in the embryo can be detected at roughly six weeks, about two weeks after a missed period. Supporters see a developing human life at that stage; opponents note that many people do not yet know they are pregnant. The underlying dispute is where, somewhere between conception and viability at around 24 weeks, the state should draw its line. In 2022, only about 42% of U.S. abortions took place at or before six weeks, so a six-week cutoff reaches most procedures.",
