    "offer": "The Native Title Act would set up a single national system — including a National Native Title Tribunal — for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander groups to apply to have their traditional rights to land and waters legally recognised. To succeed, a group must show an unbroken connection to the area under their own laws and customs, and that those rights were never extinguished by later acts such as the grant of freehold. Existing freehold and most leases are confirmed, so recognised native title would mainly cover vacant Crown land, some national parks and similar areas. Holders would gain a \"right to negotiate\" over developments like mining — but not a veto. A separate land fund would buy land for people too dispossessed to meet the connection test.",
