        "text": "Supporters argue the technology is simply too biased to aim at the public. The U.S. government's own NIST evaluation of dozens of algorithms found 10 to 100 times as many false positives for Asian and African-American faces as for white faces in one-to-one matching, echoing lab tests where commercial software misread darker-skinned women up to 34.7% of the time. Wiring such tools into everyday policing, they warn, would generate wrongful stops and arrests that fall hardest on minority residents.",
